DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
     These routines are used to get public and secret keys from the YP data‐
     base.  The ggeettsseeccrreettkkeeyy() function has an extra argument, _p_a_s_s_w_d, which
     is used to decrypt the encrypted secret key stored in the database.  Both
     routines return 1 if they are successful in finding the key, 0 otherwise.
     The keys are returned as NUL-terminated, hexadecimal strings.  If the
     password supplied to ggeettsseeccrreettkkeeyy() fails to decrypt the secret key, the
     routine will return 1 but the _s_e_c_r_e_t_k_e_y argument will be a NUL string
     (“”).

